<DocsLayout title="Domains, routing & webhooks" description="Understand automatic project subdomains, Caddy routing, Cloudflare ingress, and GitHub push delivery.">
<section><p class="overline">Routing model</p><h2>One public domain, automatic project subdomains</h2><p>Each project receives a hostname below the configured MyPaaS domain. If the configured domain is <code>mypaas.example.com</code>, a project named <code>portfolio</code> can be routed as <code>portfolio.mypaas.example.com</code>. Cloudflare Tunnel forwards the root and wildcard hostnames to Caddy; Caddy then routes dashboard/API traffic, static releases, and explicitly routed runtimes.</p><ol class="steps"><li>Cloudflare Tunnel receives public HTTPS traffic for the root and wildcard hostnames.</li><li>Caddy is the MyPaaS front door.</li><li>MyPaaS resolves the project routing identity and waits for the supported route target to be ready.</li><li>Static projects are served from their active release directory; container-backed projects are attached to the managed routing network before route activation.</li><li>Caddy configuration is reconciled from desired project state after control-plane restart.</li></ol></section>
<section><h2>Route activation is fail-closed</h2><p>MyPaaS validates the intended runtime before attaching the managed routing alias and activating the Caddy upstream. A replacement that is missing, unhealthy, or cannot be resolved onto the expected runtime path is not promoted merely because a deployment command finished.</p></section>
<section><h2>GitHub push webhooks</h2><p>Git-backed projects expose a webhook URL and per-project signing value in project settings. Add the webhook to the repository, select push events, and target the branch configured on the project.</p><p>Only valid signed pushes to the configured branch are accepted. Registry-image projects do not use Git webhooks because they do not have a Git source.</p></section>
</DocsLayout>
